## Fee Clarification: Exit Load
### Reusable Support Snippet

  • Exit load is a fee levied by the mutual fund scheme, not by the investment platform, and is applied only when units are redeemed before the scheme‑specified minimum holding period.
  • The percentage shown in the app is the fund‑defined exit‑load rate; it does not include GST, brokerage, or any other charges.
  • GST at the prevailing rate (currently 18%) is charged on the exit‑load amount, and the tax is added to the fee at the time of redemption.
  • If a scheme declares a zero‑exit‑load, no exit‑load fee is charged regardless of the redemption timing; the fee applies only when the scheme’s offer document lists a non‑zero rate.
  • For systematic investment plans (SIPs), each installment is treated as a separate investment, so the holding period and applicable exit‑load are calculated individually for each tranche.
